codex
The first residual exposed only an encoding issue: the prover knew `numVals(NS)` was empty but could not invert that helper to conclude `NS` was empty. I’m removing that unnecessary encoding and quantifying directly over symbolic `ValSeq`, guarded by a recursive “all elements are Int or Float” predicate. This preserves the full unbounded mixed-numeric domain and lets MPY’s list constructors drive induction directly.
